      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["U5"],
      "pins": ["U5.34"],
      "nets": ["LED1"],
      "observed": "U5 pin 34, P1_LED, is on net LED1, which is the 3.3V output rail; that net also contains IC1 FB, L2 output, C13, Q2 source, R2 pull-up, and U5 3.3VD pins.",
      "expected": "P1_LED is a GPIO/LED signal and should not be tied directly to the +3V3 rail. The spec's +3V3 destination list does not include U5.34.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"34\") (pinfunction \"P1_LED\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"21\") (name \"LED1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C13 +3V3 0 10u"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "+3V3 rail destinations: SKW92A module power pins (`U5.28`, `U5.29` — matching the datasheet's two dedicated `3.3VD` pins), keyboard `U4.2`, microSD `J2.4`, the gate pull-up `R2` (10 kΩ, pulling Q2's gate high/off by default), and the EPD power-switch MOSFET `Q2`'s source."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the P1_LED GPIO ever drives low, it shorts the 3.3V rail to ground through the pin; at minimum, the LED/GPIO signal cannot be controlled independently.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the specified EPD bypass capacitor value (C1 is 0.1µF/16V instead of 1µF/25V) and appears to short the SKW92A P1_LED GPIO to the 3.3V rail."
}

